# Initial Setup's Secure page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigSecureAP.cs.
#
# InitialSetup lists it at the top while no vehicle is connected (isDisConnected,
# InitialSetup.cs:176-179), so this script runs with no link: the data directory is a scratch one,
# so no link Mission Planner remembers is opened. It needs no SITL.
#
# The claims: the page is listed, shows the Designer's two groups - "Do Only Once" with Generate
# Key, "Files" with Private Key, BootLoader and Firmware and the three text boxes beside them - and
# every button is disabled. Each of the four handlers is Ed25519 key generation, key reading or
# signing (ConfigSecureAP.cs:30-111, SignedFW.cs), done in the C# by BouncyCastle; this application
# has no Ed25519 implementation, so nothing on the page can be pressed. The script clicks none of
# them; config/secure.rs's tests hold the controls to the Designer and each handler to Ed25519.

env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK

screen setup
window 1600x1200
settle 3

expect config.secure.active false
expect setup.pages ~ ConfigSecureAP
click setup-page-ConfigSecureAP
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigSecureAP
expect setup.title Secure
expect config.secure.active true
expect config.secure.groups Do Only Once,Files
expect config.secure.buttons Generate Key,Private Key,BootLoader,Firmware
expect config.secure.boxes txt_pubkey,txt_bl,txt_fwapj
expect config.secure.buttons.enabled false
expect config.secure.disabled ~ Ed25519

# Another page - the Optional Hardware heading, which fetches nothing - and Secure is no longer the
# page showing.
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigOptional
expect config.secure.active false
